   "text": "This SMILES describes the drawing as a rifamycin-type ansamycin whose naphthoquinone core is fused to a phenoxazine ring that carries a 2-(imidazol-1-yl)ethoxy group. I wrote it by reading the structure region by region. I took the macrocycle stereochemistry and double-bond geometry from the known natural rifamycin pattern (as in rifampicin), not by re-deriving each wedge and hash from the image, so those assignments are less certain than the connectivity.\n\n- **Ansa chain:** The NH amide carries a dienoyl unit, C(=O)\u2013C(CH3)=CH\u2013CH=CH. This leads into the polyketide chain with its secondary methyls, two OH groups, the OAc and the OMe, and ends in the enol ether O\u2013CH=CH.\n- **Furanone:** The quaternary carbon bears a methyl and is bonded to the ring oxygen, the C=O and the enol-ether oxygen.\n- **Core:** The aromatic ring has a methyl and an OH, and it is fused to a quinone ring with a C=O next to the NH-bearing carbon. That quinone ring is fused in turn to the phenoxazine (an N= and an O bridge to the benzo ring).\n- **Side chain:** The benzo ring carries O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013N(imidazole).\n\nI checked the ring closures and valences by hand, and the macrocycle closes through ring label 1.\n\nSMILES: C[C@H]1/C=C/C=C(\\C(=O)NC2=C3Oc4cc(OCCn5ccnc5)ccc4N=C3C6=C(C2=O)C(O)=C(C)C7=C6C(=O)[C@](C)(O7)O/C=C/[C@@H]([C@H]([C@H]([C@@H]([C@@H]([C@@H]([C@H]1O)C)O)C)OC(=O)C)C)OC)/C"
